caledonian.en:
a. Of or pertaining to Caledonia or Scotland; Scottish;
   Scotch.
n. A native or inhabitant of Caledonia or Scotland.

canonry.en:
n. pl. A benefice or prebend in a cathedral or collegiate
   church; a right to a place in chapter and to a portion of its revenues;
   the dignity or emoluments of a canon.

capitally.en:
adv. In a way involving the forfeiture of the head or life;
   as, to punish capitally.
adv. In a capital manner; excellently.

cathetus.en:
n. One line or radius falling perpendicularly on another;
   as, the catheti of a right-angled triangle, that is, the two sides that
   include the right angle.

choicely.en:
adv. With care in choosing; with nice regard to preference.
adv. In a preferable or excellent manner; excellently;
   eminently.

churchmanships.en:
plural of churchmanship
n. The state or quality of being a churchman;
   attachment to the church.

circumstanced.en:
p. a. Placed in a particular position or condition;
   situated.
p. a. Governed by events or circumstances.

cirrhotics.en:
plural of cirrhotic
a. Pertaining to, caused by, or affected with, cirrhosis;
   as, cirrhotic degeneration; a cirrhotic liver.

cobaltic.en:
a. Pertaining to, derived from, or containing, cobalt; --
   said especially of those compounds in which cobalt has higher valence;
   as, cobaltic oxide.

colorado.en:
n. a state in west central United States in the Rocky Mountains
n. a river in Texas; flows southeast into the Gulf of Mexico
n. an important river in the southwestern United States; rises in the Rocky Mountains of northern Colorado and flows southwest through Utah into Arizona (where it flows through the Grand Canyon) and then southward through the southern tip of Nevada, then forming the border between California and Arizona and finally into Mexico where it empties into the Gulf of California;

columbic.en:
a. Pertaining to, or containing, columbium or niobium;
   niobic.
a. Pertaining to, or derived from, the columbo root.

commentation.en:
n. The act or process of commenting or criticising;
   exposition.
n. The result of the labors of a commentator.

commorancy.en:
n. A dwelling or ordinary residence in a place;
   habitation.
n. Residence temporarily, or for a short time.

contexture.en:
n. The arrangement and union of the constituent parts of a
   thing; a weaving together of parts; structural character of a thing;
   system; constitution; texture.

contrariants.en:
plural of contrariant
a. Contrary; opposed; antagonistic; inconsistent;
   contradictory.

coquimbite.en:
n. A mineral consisting principally of sulphate of iron;
   white copperas; -- so called because found in the province of Coquimbo,
   Chili.

crasis.en:
n. A mixture of constituents, as of the blood; constitution;
   temperament.
n. A contraction of two vowels (as the final and initial
   vowels of united words) into one long vowel, or into a diphthong;
   synaeresis; as, cogo for coago.

crookes tube.en:
A vacuum tube in which the exhaustion is carried to a
   very high degree, with the production of a distinct class of effects;
   -- so called from W. Crookes who introduced it.

cuirassed.en:
a. Wearing a cuirass.
a. Having a covering of bony plates, resembling a cuirass;
   -- said of certain fishes.

currentness.en:
n. The quality of being current; currency; circulation;
   general reception.
n. Easiness of pronunciation; fluency.

curtana.en:
n. The pointless sword carried before English monarchs at
   their coronation, and emblematically considered as the sword of mercy;
   -- also called the sword of Edward the Confessor.
